WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:02.620
- [Narrator] What if I told you,

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.883
you can literally eat fire?

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.629
Yes, literally.

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:10.212
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.790
In India, paan is a huge culinary darling

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.953
that's been around for centuries.

00:00:18.953 --> 00:00:22.000
It's a snack usually eaten after a meal

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.870
to help with digestion.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.390
It consists of a betel
of leaf that's wrapped

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:28.720
around all kinds of different fillings,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.830
like nuts, fennel, cardamom, fruits,

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.603
chocolate, or even meat.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.130
You can find it anywhere.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.860
But a small street food shack in New Delhi

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.593
is sparking a revolution.

00:01:05.377 --> 00:01:06.529
- [Narrator] All right, then.

00:01:06.529 --> 00:01:08.400
But back to the revolution he's sparking.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.240
Recently, he had an idea that
would reignite the classic

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.093
Indian snack his shack was famous for.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.270
- [Narrator] I have a
burning question for you:

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.517
Is it safe to eat?

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.080
- [Narrator] You're really
bringing on the heat.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.890
OK, that was a slow-burner.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.980
I was just warming up.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.759
OK, OK, we've already
burned too much time.

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:07.759
(crickets chirping)

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:19.630
- [Narrator] So, there you have it.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.729
India's hottest trend.

00:02:21.729 --> 00:02:24.396
(upbeat music)

